WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.837
Grain means what one row represents.

00:00:02.837 --> 00:00:06.807
A sales fact table may have one row per transaction.

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:10.912
After grouping, the grain may become one product-month.

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:15.942
After pivoting months into columns, the grain may become one product.

00:00:15.942 --> 00:00:21.687
If you cannot state the row grain, it is difficult to know whether a reshape is correct.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:27.512
Reshaping can change grain, so define it before and after the transformation.

00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:34.452
A source may have one row per patient-measurement, while a pivoted result has one row per patient.

00:00:34.452 --> 00:00:40.407
If multiple source rows map to the same target cell, you must decide how they are aggregated;

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.714
otherwise information can be lost.
